    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="1036" n="1020" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1020"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/5–1549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Legation in Syria </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-17T19:00:00-04:00">May 17, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>217. Ur 281 May 13 third para. Connection possibility US representations re
                    Israeli-Arab armistice agreements. Dept has worked closely with Bunche and, as
                    in case Deptel 209 May 12, has not instructed US reps make representations until
                    so requested by Bunche. Dept appreciates ur suggestion but view fact Bunche has
                    the responsibility for conduct negots desires that question possibility and
                    timing US representations be handled through prior consultation with him as
                    heretofore.</p>
                <pb facs="1037" n="1021" xml:id="pg1021"/>
                <p>View further revision Bunche proposal Dept concurs representation to Syrian Govt
                    present time not desirable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
